      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-14T11:30:16.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS in line with expectations, revenues disappoint",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹61.15 (up from ₹54.76 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹39.7b (up 5.8% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹10.4b (up 12% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 26% (up from 25% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue missed analyst estimates by 1.6%. Earnings per share (EPS) were mostly in line with analyst estimates. Revenue is forecast to grow 8.2% p.a. on average during the next 2 years, compared to a 12% growth forecast for the Pharmaceuticals industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 23% per year whereas the company’s share price has increased by 24% per year.",
